        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(qa-lab): keep capture preview truncation UTF-16 safe",
        "body": "Fixes an unsafe UTF-16 truncation in the QA Lab web UI capture preview path.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\n`extensions/qa-lab/web/src/ui-render.ts` truncates long captured scalar values for display using raw `.slice(0, 280)` for the head and `.slice(-80)` for the tail. If the captured text contains a supplementary Unicode character (e.g. an emoji) that straddles either boundary, the preview ends up with a dangling surrogate half.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplaced the two raw `.slice()` calls with `sliceUtf16Safe` from the plugin SDK, which handles surrogate boundaries correctly. The scalar redactor is now exported so the regression tests can exercise the exact truncation path without rendering the full UI.\n\nTo keep the QA Lab web bundle browser-safe, `src/plugin-sdk/text-utility-runtime.ts` now imports `sliceUtf16Safe`/`truncateUtf16Safe` directly from `@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice` instead of re-exporting them through `src/utils.js` (which imports `node:fs`/`node:os`/`node:path`). This avoids pulling Node.js built-ins into the Vite browser bundle for this helper.\n\n## User Impact\n\nQA Lab capture previews remain valid and readable when captured request/response bodies or fields contain emoji or other non-BMP characters.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused regression test: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/qa-lab/web/src/ui-render.test.ts --run` passes (9/9 tests).\n- The new tests place an emoji immediately after the 279-code-unit head boundary and immediately before the 79-code-unit tail boundary, asserting that the result contains no dangling high/low surrogates.\n- `git diff --check` passes.\n- `pnpm exec oxfmt --check` passes for the touched files.\n- `pnpm qa:lab:build` completes successfully after the browser-safe import change:\n\n```text\n$ pnpm qa:lab:build\n$ vite build --config extensions/qa-lab/web/vite.config.ts\nvite v8.1.3 building client environment for production...\n✓ 85 modules transformed.\nrendering chunks...\ncomputing gzip size...\nextensions/qa-lab/web/dist/index.html                   0.44 kB │ gzip:  0.28 kB\nextensions/qa-lab/web/dist/assets/index-BlQ-kj4N.css   57.47 kB │ gzip:  9.70 kB\nextensions/qa-lab/web/dist/assets/index-DAN1kyBx.js   285.85 kB │ gzip: 77.61 kB\n\n✓ built in 331ms\n```",
        "branch": "fix/qa-lab-web-capture-utf16-safe",
        "head_sha": "06058a7c43eb02027a761097c97ff8c5f46f93f6",
